    "lambda_th": 0.0,
    "delta_w_definition": "delta_w = n_g / (alpha * n_r_w) - 1 on cells with raw random CIC count >= NR_MIN; alpha = sum(n_g)/sum(n_r_w) over supported cells; delta_w = 0 elsewhere (zero-padding). The n_r_w-weighted mean of delta_w over the support is 0 by construction (alpha normalization), addressing the integral-constraint family; the UNWEIGHTED per-cell mean is +1.15 (measured), reflecting the radial-profile mismatch between the zall GALAXY parent and the BGS_BRIGHT clustering selection (low-z cells hold more parent galaxies per random than high-z cells). The k=0 mode is zeroed in the Poisson inversion, so the offset does not enter the tidal classification.",
